Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage for this task  

• `date`: filter records to the years 2019, 2020, 2021 (EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) IN (…) )  
• `category_name`: group liquor sales by category to compute averages  
• `state_bottle_retail`: retail price paid by the store for a single bottle; part of per‑liter price calculation  
• `bottle_volume_ml`: bottle size in millilitres; part of per‑liter price calculation  
• `category` (numeric code): can also be used for grouping or as a join key if you prefer codes instead of names  
• `sale_dollars`, `bottles_sold`, `volume_sold_liters`: not required here, but can be useful for cross‑checks  
• `invoice_and_item_number`: unique row id—useful only if you need to de‑duplicate data (not required in the examples)  

Typical conditions that will be used  

• Year filter: `EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date)=2021` (or 2019, 2020)  
• Top‑10 categories in 2021: `ORDER BY avg_price_per_liter DESC LIMIT 10`  
• Price‑per‑liter calculation: `state_bottle_retail / (bottle_volume_ml/1000.0)`  

Below are ten example BigQuery SQL queries—from very simple inspection queries to the final query answering the task.  
Each query is annotated and limited where appropriate.  

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at raw rows in the Iowa liquor sales table.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect which calendar years are present in the data.
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) AS sales_year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
ORDER BY sales_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: List a sample of distinct liquor categories.
SELECT DISTINCT category_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
ORDER BY category_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Count transactions per category in 2021.
SELECT category_name,
       COUNT(*) AS txn_cnt_2021
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2021
GROUP BY category_name
ORDER BY txn_cnt_2021 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Show per‑liter retail price for a small sample of 2021 rows.
SELECT category_name,
       state_bottle_retail,
       bottle_volume_ml,
       state_bottle_retail / (bottle_volume_ml/1000.0) AS price_per_liter
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2021
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Average per‑liter retail price per category for 2021.
SELECT category_name,
       AVG(state_bottle_retail / (bottle_volume_ml/1000.0)) AS avg_price_per_liter_2021
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2021
GROUP BY category_name
ORDER BY avg_price_per_liter_2021 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Top‑10 categories in 2021 by average per‑liter retail price.
WITH cat21 AS (
  SELECT category_name,
         AVG(state_bottle_retail / (bottle_volume_ml/1000.0)) AS avg_price_per_liter_2021
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2021
  GROUP BY category_name
)
SELECT *
FROM cat21
ORDER BY avg_price_per_liter_2021 DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Compute average per‑liter retail price per category for 2019‑2021.
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) AS sales_year,
       category_name,
       AVG(state_bottle_retail / (bottle_volume_ml/1000.0)) AS avg_price_per_liter
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) BETWEEN 2019 AND 2021
GROUP BY sales_year, category_name
ORDER BY category_name, sales_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Keep only the categories that are top‑10 (by price) in 2021 and show their 2019‑2021 averages.
WITH cat21 AS (
  SELECT category_name,
         AVG(state_bottle_retail / (bottle_volume_ml/1000.0)) AS avg_price_per_liter_2021
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2021
  GROUP BY category_name
  ORDER BY avg_price_per_liter_2021 DESC
  LIMIT 10
)
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM s.`date`) AS sales_year,
       s.category_name,
       AVG(s.state_bottle_retail / (s.bottle_volume_ml/1000.0)) AS avg_price_per_liter
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales` AS s
JOIN cat21 USING (category_name)
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM s.`date`) BETWEEN 2019 AND 2021
GROUP BY sales_year, category_name
ORDER BY category_name, sales_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final answer – top‑10 2021 categories with their average per‑liter retail prices for 2019‑2021.
WITH cat21 AS (
  -- identify top 10 categories in 2021
  SELECT category_name,
         AVG(state_bottle_retail / (bottle_volume_ml/1000.0)) AS avg_price_per_liter_2021
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2021
  GROUP BY category_name
  ORDER BY avg_price_per_liter_2021 DESC
  LIMIT 10
),
yr_avgs AS (
  -- compute yearly averages for those categories
  SELECT category_name,
         EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) AS sales_year,
         AVG(state_bottle_retail / (bottle_volume_ml/1000.0)) AS avg_price_per_liter
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) BETWEEN 2019 AND 2021
    AND category_name IN (SELECT category_name FROM cat21)
  GROUP BY category_name, sales_year
)
-- pivot so each year is a column
SELECT category_name,
       MAX(IF(sales_year=2019, avg_price_per_liter, NULL)) AS avg_price_per_liter_2019,
       MAX(IF(sales_year=2020, avg_price_per_liter, NULL)) AS avg_price_per_liter_2020,
       MAX(IF(sales_year=2021, avg_price_per_liter, NULL)) AS avg_price_per_liter_2021
FROM yr_avgs
GROUP BY category_name
ORDER BY avg_price_per_liter_2021 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
